    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Ppfuey4GbjRSrz2HEtS393)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on current `main` (after #517); independent of the other open PRs.\n- Touches `sp-bibprocess` / `sp-academic.org` (the lint part), so it may conflict with other open PRs on the same section.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Organisations as authors** (`The editors`, `Mute Collective`):\n  - The `Last, First` rewrite no longer touches names that look like an organisation (`sp-bibtex-organisation-patterns`: `The ...`, Collective, Committee, Association, University, Institute, Press, Group, editors, ...). They are flagged instead.\n  - New step 0b of `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors` (also `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-organisations`): per batch, `o` = organisations (written as `{{Mute Collective}}`), `P` = persons (converted in step 1), `e` = each name, `s`, `d`, `u`, `q`; `n`/`p` still browse the report.\n  - In the author and lint reports, `o` and `P` mark a name of the entry at point (any name, also one the patterns miss); the report redraws.\n  - Answers are remembered in `sp-bibtex-organisations-file` (`:organisations`, `:persons`), so they are not asked again. A remembered organisation is wrapped automatically, and a name already damaged to `Collective, Mute` is repaired.\n  - Names in braces are skipped by the typo, same-surname, prefix and merge steps.\n- **BibTeX accents** (`C{\\'e}sar Bola{\\~n}o`):\n  - Matching the author notes decodes the accents, so it finds the note `César Bolaño`. The field keeps its escapes and the braces survive (`Bola{\\~n}o, C{\\'e}sar`).\n  - `sp-bibtex-names-unicode` (off by default) writes `Bolaño, César` instead.\n  - Aliases added to a note are written in Unicode.\n  - The space of an unbraced accent (`\\c c`) no longer splits a name.\n- No note is created by the lint (unchanged). `CHANGELOG.org` not edited. Docs updated as bullet lists in `sp-academic.org`, tangled to `sp-bibprocess.el`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- 16 new tests in `tests/sp-bibprocess-lint-test.el`; Emacs 29.3 in batch: all 128 pass.\n- Not run on the real `.bib` files or in the interactive config (keys `o`/`P` in the report, and the echo-area help line, are untested).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors` on a `.bib` with `author = {The editors}` and `{Mute Collective}`: neither shows `→ Last, First`; step 0b lists them\n- [ ] In step 0b, `o` writes `{{The editors}}` and `{{Mute Collective}}`; the later steps leave them alone\n- [ ] Run again: they are not asked again\n- [ ] `P` on a flagged real person (e.g. `Anna Press`): step 1 converts it to `Press, Anna`, and it is not flagged again\n- [ ] `e` asks name by name, once per distinct name\n- [ ] In the report, `o` on an entry whose name the patterns miss marks it, and the report shows `→ {Name}`\n- [ ] The echo-area help line shows `o`/`P` in the report; `n`/`p` still move\n- [ ] `author = {C{\\'e}sar Bola{\\~n}o}` with a person note `César Bolaño`: shows `→ Bola{\\~n}o, C{\\'e}sar`, no typo suggestion\n- [ ] With `sp-bibtex-names-unicode` on: `→ Bolaño, César`\n- [ ] The `Variants of one author` step ignores `{{Mute Collective}}`\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBFBRHmoAuFaTY7mup)_",
